        <paragraph>For functions $$f(x) = x + 2$$ and $$g(x) = 3x^{2} - 2x + 4,$$ find ⓐ $$\left( {f \cdot g} \right)(x)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {f \cdot g} \right)(-1)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="279" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>For functions $$f(x) = x - 1$$ and $$g(x) = 4x^{2} + 3x - 5,$$ find ⓐ $$\left( {f \cdot g} \right)(x)$$ ⓑ $$\left( {f \cdot g} \right)(-2)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$(f\cdot g)(x)=4x3-x2-8x+5(f\cdot g)(x)=4x3-x2-8x+5$$ ⓑ $$(f\cdot g)(-2)=-15(f\cdot g)(-2)=-15$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
